# 🌍 English Contemplation
## **When Knowing Becomes Love and Love Becomes Wisdom**
There is a difference between knowing about God and realizing the Truth.
There is also a difference between speaking of devotion and allowing love to transform one's life.
Scriptural learning can remain intellectual.
Devotional emotion can remain temporary.
Neither information nor emotion alone guarantees liberation.
Yet authentic knowledge and mature devotion need not be enemies.
Knowledge asks:
**Who am I, beyond the changing body and mind?**
Devotion asks:
**To whom does this life belong?**
Knowledge loosens false identification.
Devotion loosens possessiveness.
Selfless action loosens the demand for reward.
Meditation cultivates steadiness.
And genuine spiritual maturity becomes visible in humility, compassion, clarity and freedom from selfish attachment.
The philosophical traditions may disagree about the final relationship between the individual soul and God.
Those differences deserve respect.
But a sincere seeker can still learn from their shared emphasis on purification, discipline, love and truthfulness.
The aim is not to win an argument between knowledge and devotion.
It is to discover whether either has truly transformed the one who argues.
**When knowledge becomes pride, it has lost its purpose.**
**When devotion becomes possessiveness, it has forgotten love.**
And when both become humble, clear and selfless, spiritual life begins to flower.
